      blocks: [
        ["lead", "Everything below is live at portal.gaza40plus.co.uk, not planned."],
        ["h", "01", "For the student"],
        ["cards", [{ t: "Onboarding with three stacked gates", body: "Email verification blocks the whole API for self registered accounts. Community guideline approval is a consent record and blocks offers, queries and chat. Profile approval blocks offer management. Each gate exists for a reason and they fire in that order, so review time is only spent on verified cases." }, { t: "Conditional profile requirements", body: "A student whose passport status is invalid, lost or never had one is not asked to upload a passport. The absence is recorded as a fact and there is a query category for exactly that problem. In an ordinary admissions system a missing passport is an incomplete form. Here it is a case type." }, { t: "Offer submission with real preconditions", body: "Submitting requires an offer letter document, and a scholarship letter as well if a scholarship is being claimed. Submission flips the status to under review and sets a lock, so an administrator is never reviewing a moving target." }, { t: "Queries with a named owner", body: "The student picks a category, the system derives the region from their own offer and assigns a specific person who gets notified. They can see the thread and whether it is resolved, which is the one thing a WhatsApp message cannot tell them." }]],
        ["h", "02", "For the reviewers and coordinators"],
        ["list", "Offer review", ["A queue scoped to one country, filled by the offer's university country rather than by where any student lives", "Approve, request changes or reject, with the decision and the actor written to the audit log", "Optional mentor assignment on the offer, typically someone affiliated with that university", "A field level diff on any edit to an already approved offer, so the reviewer reads what moved instead of the whole record again"]],
        ["list", "Student review", ["Profile review with an explicit transition map rather than a free status field, so an approved profile cannot be pushed back to draft by accident", "Passport number, national ID number and passport expiry stripped out of the response for mentors and regional admins even though the record was loaded to build it", "Reviewers can upload documents on behalf of a student, restricted to non offer types"]],
        ["h", "03", "Files, money and exports"],
        ["table", ["Feature", "The actual mechanic"], [["Private documents", "Cloudflare R2 with random keys, no public URL anywhere in the system, streamed through an authenticated endpoint after four checks, audited on every download, superseded rather than overwritten on re upload"], ["Upload limits", "5MB per document and 1MB for a signature, matched by the Nginx body limit, because Nginx rejecting a phone camera upload before Node ever saw it was a real production incident"], ["Funding engine", "One server side function reading a rules row from the database, amortising one time grants across the course, and returning the source of every figure next to the figure"], ["CSV export", "A background job, not a response. A job record is created, a runner streams the data in cursor paginated batches of a thousand to a temp file, uploads it to R2, and the UI polls for a signed link"], ["Export safety", "The authorization scope is frozen into the job at creation so a permission change mid run cannot widen it, jobs can be cancelled between batches, jobs interrupted by a restart are marked failed at boot, and a daily cron expires old exports and deletes the objects"], ["Audit log", "Append only, roughly thirty actions, recording actor, IP, user agent and the shape of what happened. It records that review notes were provided, never the notes, and which fields changed, never the values"]]],
        ["h", "04", "Communication, kept as two systems"],
        ["p", "Query messages and chat are separate on purpose, and the reason is retention. A query thread is part of the case record: permanent, audited, and locked once the query is resolved. Chat is coordination: direct and group messaging with attachments and a seven day retention window, because holding less conversation about vulnerable people is better than holding more. Different retention is the whole reason they are two systems rather than one with a flag on it."],
        ["list", "How chat permissions actually work", ["Master admins can reach anyone and post into any conversation without being a member", "Regional admins can reach each other and the mentors in their own region", "Mentors cannot message other mentors", "Group creation is restricted to administrators, and adding a student to a group requires that the student has a case in that administrator's region", "Student chat sits behind an application config flag, so the organization can turn it off without a deploy"]],
        ["p", "The realtime transport is HTTP polling rather than WebSockets. That is worse on paper. It survives restrictive networks and keeps the secure session cookie intact through the proxy, which matters more than the benchmark for the people actually using it."],
        ["h", "05", "The parts nobody sees"],
        ["list", null, ["Announcements scoped to global plus the regions a student's own offers imply, so a UK notice does not reach someone with no UK case", "Notifications by email and in app on the events that change someone's obligations: profile decisions, offer decisions, assignment, escalation", "Rate limiting on the API generally, on authentication, and separately on uploads", "Session tokens in httpOnly cookies with separate access and refresh secrets, both validated at startup rather than silently defaulted", "Cross site request protection on every mutating request", "Dashboard reads issued as one parallel batch rather than in sequence, and summary counts done as database aggregations rather than by loading rows", "Bilingual English and Arabic with a right to left layout switch, reaching down to Arabic labels on the configuration options the organization edits"]],
        ["note", "One thing I will not dress up: there are no automated tests, and lint is a TypeScript typecheck. For a system whose main security property is data isolation enforced at nineteen separate call sites, that is the largest structural risk in the project, and closing it comes before any individual fix."],
      ],
